Package: LogicComm
Type: Package
Title: Logic-Based Cell-Cell Communication Analysis for Multi-Sample scRNA-seq
Version: 0.10.2
Date: 2026-06-05
Authors@R: person("LogicComm", "Developer", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "dev@logiccomm.io")
Author: LogicComm Developer
Maintainer: LogicComm Developer <dev@logiccomm.io>
Description: Identifies cell-cell communication signals by converting single-cell
    gene expression into Relative Expression Ordering (REO) binary logic states,
    then detecting ligand-receptor Logic Consensus Scores (LCS) across cell
    neighborhoods. Designed for scalable multi-sample comparison, such as case
    versus control cohorts, without requiring cell type pre-annotation. Supports
    cell-type-resolved communication summaries, weighted graph scoring,
    signaling-role centrality with confidence labels, bootstrap/null diagnostics,
    receiver-response logic scoring, spatial and pseudotime communication
    modules, sample-level quasibinomial differential modeling, publication-ready
    specificity scoring, permutation-null diagnostics, role-evidence interpretation,
    rank-aware REO evidence, threshold-stability scoring, report helpers,
    BPCells on-disk matrices, and Rcpp high-performance computation.
